<title>USA: Lawyers Title Corp Q1 net income falls.</title>
<headline>Lawyers Title Corp Q1 net income falls.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended March 31</p>
<p>							1997	     1996</p>
<p> Premiums				     $102,735	  $94,720</p>
<p> This search, escrow and other	    24,435	   22,749</p>
<p> Investment Income			     4,136	    5,345</p>
<p>						   131,306	  122,814</p>
<p> Salaries and employee benefits	   46,916	   43,287</p>
<p> Agents' commissions			  44,711	   37,133</p>
<p>Provision for policy and contract claims</p>
<p>						     6,980	    6,286</p>
<p> General, administrative and other	31,615	   29,391</p>
<p>						   130,222	  116,097</p>
<p> Operating income before taxes	     1,084	    6,717</p>
<p> Income taxes					237	    2,196</p>
<p> Net income					  847	    4,521</p>
<p> Earnings per share			     0.10	     0.51</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding		  8,900	    8,887</p>
<p>		    (Dollars in thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q1 included $2.2 million of capital gains before taxes, while there were no significant capital gains in Q1 1997.</p>
<p>Q1 1997 operating margin, before claims and investment income, was 3.1 percent compared to 6.5 percent in Q1 1996.</p>
<p>The margin in 1997 was impacted by an increase in average agents' commission rates of 1.3 percent, which reflects continued competition for agency business.</p>
</text>
